{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And a new king arose.</b> This is Pharaoh the first. They said to him: Come, let us make war against this nation. He said to them: Until now we have lived from what is theirs — how can we make war against them? He did not listen to them. They deposed him from his throne for three months. When he saw this, he said to them: I will listen to you. Therefore it is written ויקם ['arose']." "<b>Who did not know Joseph.</b> Rabbi Yehuda ben Levi said: A parable — to one who stoned the king's icon. They seized him and released him. The next day he stoned the king himself. So too Pharaoh: at first he said, 'who did not know Joseph,' and in the end he said, ״לא ידעתי את ה׳״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:25.948640974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}